{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"9ff5fead5a073518","type":"group","x":60,"y":0,"width":2620,"height":280,"label":"Untitled group"},
		{"id":"pl00000000000000","type":"text","text":"**Phase 0 · cheap check** *(in sim)*\nBefore building anything: is there time to react, and can we recover the physics?\n\n**✓ go / no-go:** react window ≥ 31 ms · physics error ≤ 15%","x":1300,"y":1181,"width":560,"height":139,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"pl00000000000001","type":"text","text":"**Step 1 · falsify** *(3 in parallel)*\nOne cheap test per coupling: does predicting the push beat ignoring it?\n\n**✓ go / no-go:** ≥ 5 pp better where the push is largest","x":1300,"y":1360,"width":560,"height":120,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"pl00000000000002","type":"text","text":"**Step 2 · ground**\nMeasure the real physics on the robot (system-ID).\n\n**✓ go / no-go:** ≤ 15% error · beats random-tuning · ≥ 80% kept","x":1300,"y":1520,"width":560,"height":120,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"pl00000000000003","type":"text","text":"**Step 3 · build CoWAM**\nOne model that predicts the push, with no force sensor.\n\n**✓ go / no-go:** within 2× of a sensor-equipped baseline","x":1300,"y":1680,"width":560,"height":120,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"pl00000000000004","type":"text","text":"**Step 4 · verify**\nCheck the predicted push = the real push, on hardware.\n\n**✓ go / no-go:** R² ≥ 0.70 · no forgetting","x":1300,"y":1840,"width":560,"height":120,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"pl00000000000005","type":"text","text":"**Step 5 · deploy**\nRun live on the real humanoid (H1 / G1).\n\n**✓ go / no-go:** real-time at ≥ 30 Hz","x":1300,"y":1999,"width":560,"height":121,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a300000000000001","type":"text","text":"The coupling head (predict A+C wrench, factor B) **plugs onto any WAM backbone**, grounded (S2R.B) and verified (EAI.B):","x":2440,"y":1140,"width":640,"height":80},
		{"id":"a300000000000004","type":"text","text":"## CoWAM — my idea\n**Predict the arm-base-leg push ahead of time, make it real, then check it.**\n*6 research clusters (chosen from ~77 ideas) → a better whole-body humanoid.*","x":2440,"y":1240,"width":640,"height":120,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a300000000000002","type":"text","text":"```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    O[\"observation\"] --> Bk[\"WAM backbone (swappable)\"]\n    P[\"proprio + commanded q̈_arm + est. F_ext\"] --> CC[\"coupling-conditioned latent (added)\"]\n    Bk --> Z[\"latent z_t\"]\n    CC --> Z\n    Z --> W[\"SHARED WRENCH HEAD (added)<br/>δ_base (A) + J_ext^T F_ext (C), per contact mode\"]\n    Z --> AH[\"autoregressive action head (added)<br/>base→torso→arm (B)\"]\n    W --> AH\n    style CC fill:#e8fde8,stroke:#27ae60\n    style W fill:#e8fde8,stroke:#27ae60\n    style AH fill:#e8fde8,stroke:#27ae60\n    style Bk fill:#eeeeee,stroke:#888888\n```","x":2440,"y":1380,"width":640,"height":720},
		{"id":"a300000000000003","type":"text","text":"*Backbone-agnostic: the three **green** modules are the contribution — a plug-in on **any** WAM backbone. The backbone grid (DINO-WM / UWM / V-JEPA / Cosmos / a PPO floor) proves the lift is the **coupling term, not the backbone**.*","x":2440,"y":2120,"width":640,"height":100},
		{"id":"a300000000000051","type":"text","text":"**S2R.B2 · AMORTI**\n[[2603.01151|D-REX]] + [[2603.23973|SLAT-Phys]] + [[2410.20357|Dyn-as-Prompts]]\n*Guess a new object's physical properties in one shot, no tuning loop.*","x":3620,"y":1380,"width":320,"height":140},
		{"id":"a300000000000052","type":"text","text":"**S2R.B3 · FideliGate**\n[[2403.03949|RialTo]] + [[2504.03597|Real-is-Sim]] + [[2604.13645|CFG-ADDA]]\n*Only trust sim-made data when the picture matches reality closely.*","x":3960,"y":1380,"width":320,"height":138},
		{"id":"a300000000000053","type":"text","text":"**S2R.B4 · CLaRe**\n[[2304.14369|NCLaw]] + [[2508.01112|MASIV]] + [[2603.22039|RAFL]]\n*Learn the material's rule, not just its numbers, so it holds on new cases.*","x":4300,"y":1380,"width":320,"height":138},
		{"id":"a300000000000061","type":"text","text":"**EAI.B2 · CALM**\n[[2606.03385|GTP-FA]] + [[2506.21669|SEEA-R1]] + [[2508.19236|MemoryVLA]]\n*Remember why it failed, and fix the right part.*","x":3620,"y":1640,"width":320,"height":140},
		{"id":"a300000000000062","type":"text","text":"**EAI.B3 · ElastiVote**\n[[2507.05116|VOTE]] + [[2605.08799|ElasticFlow]] + [[2605.29438|ElegantVLA]]\n*Run fast enough (>=30 Hz) by recomputing only when needed.*","x":3960,"y":1640,"width":320,"height":138},
		{"id":"a300000000000063","type":"text","text":"**EAI.B4 · GSE-Null**\n[[2602.21919|Null-Space]] + [[2603.02224|Subspace-Geom]] + [[2605.06175|VLA-GSE]]\n*Learn new tasks without forgetting the old skills.*","x":4300,"y":1640,"width":320,"height":160},
		{"id":"a300000000000010","type":"text","text":"**WB.A1 · CoReWA**\n[[2604.07993|HEX]] + [[2509.21231|SEEC]] + [[2506.14278|Heavy-Limbs]]\n*Predict the push the arm puts on the base before it moves; feed it to the gate + controller.*","x":3280,"y":320,"width":320,"height":140},
		{"id":"a300000000000020","type":"text","text":"**WB.B1 · KCFlow**\n[[2503.05652|BRS]] + [[2507.01961|AC-DiT]] + [[2602.23024|InCoM]]\n*Test when letting the arm guide the base beats moving the base first.*","x":3280,"y":580,"width":320,"height":140},
		{"id":"ck00000000000003","type":"text","text":"### WB.C · force-load","x":3280,"y":760,"width":220,"height":60,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a300000000000030","type":"text","text":"**WB.C1 · PROWL**\n[[2505.06776|FALCON]] + [[2201.03871|ALMA]] + [[2606.16542|ADAPT]]\n*Sense an incoming load and brace the legs before it peaks.*","x":3280,"y":840,"width":320,"height":140},
		{"id":"ck00000000000002","type":"text","text":"### WB.B · base↔arm","x":3280,"y":500,"width":220,"height":60,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"ck00000000000001","type":"text","text":"### WB.A · arm↔leg","x":3280,"y":240,"width":220,"height":60,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"ck00000000000004","type":"text","text":"### WAM.A · predict","x":3280,"y":1020,"width":220,"height":60,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a300000000000040","type":"text","text":"**WAM.A1 · GROVER**\n[[2605.20752|GaussianDream]] + [[2602.10098|VLA-JEPA]] + [[2605.06222|FFDC-WAM]]\n*Train a rich inner world-view with a 3D teacher, then run it light.*","x":3280,"y":1100,"width":320,"height":160},
		{"id":"ck00000000000005","type":"text","text":"### S2R.B · ground","x":3280,"y":1300,"width":220,"height":60,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a300000000000050","type":"text","text":"**S2R.B1 · SENSE-T**\n[[2503.17973|PhysTwin]] + [[2511.04665|Real-to-Sim GS]] + [[2603.01151|D-REX]]\n*Measure exactly where the simulator differs from the real robot, in one pass.*","x":3280,"y":1380,"width":320,"height":140},
		{"id":"ck00000000000006","type":"text","text":"### EAI.B · verify","x":3280,"y":1560,"width":220,"height":60,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a300000000000060","type":"text","text":"**EAI.B1 · CIC**\n[[2606.05773|PiL-World]] + [[2606.18610|SC3-Eval]] + [[2605.29360|MiraBench]]\n*A score that checks the robot's imagination matches what really happens.*","x":3280,"y":1640,"width":320,"height":160},
		{"id":"loopnote00000001","type":"text","text":"↺ **The payoff:** a better whole-body humanoid — back to the goal.","x":3570,"y":1900,"width":760,"height":64,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a300000000000042","type":"text","text":"**WAM.A3 · DUET-WM**\n[[2605.06388|Semantic-LDM-WM]] + [[2503.00653|DC-MPC]] + [[2505.04999|CLAM]]\n*Split the world-view into a smooth part + a detail part, used only when needed.*","x":3960,"y":1100,"width":320,"height":160},
		{"id":"a800000000000001","type":"text","text":"**What I'm asking — your endorsement of the direction.**\nThe shape: 3 coupling clusters (arm↔legs, base↔arm, holding a load) as the core, with 3 mechanism clusters (predict, ground, verify) that support them.\n\n1. Is **predicting the coupling ahead of time** the right bet across these 6 clusters?\n2. The first experiments are cheap, run in parallel, and check themselves (no new data) — **which clusters should I do first?**\n\n*What I most want from this meeting: an early read on the idea and the cluster set.*","x":60,"y":3230,"width":860,"height":260,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a600000000000000","type":"text","text":"*Speaker note: I test only on humanoid benchmarks — the same ones the source papers use. A tabletop-arm benchmark wouldn't test a whole-body humanoid.*","x":60,"y":2600,"width":1760,"height":62},
		{"id":"a600000000000001","type":"text","text":"**Arm↔legs — balance, disturbance, whole-body moves** 🟧 *main test*\n[[2403.10506|HumanoidBench]] (standard) · [[2603.20147|AGILE]] · [[2606.17833|HumanoidArena]] · [[2503.05652|BRS]] (Galaxea R1) · [[2506.09366|SkillBench]] · [[2506.13751|LeVERB-Bench]] · [[2308.14636|Disturbance-Rejection]] + [[2404.19173|Single-Contact++]] (Digit impact) · [[2602.13656|KungFuAthlete]] · [[2508.19926|FARM]] · [[2602.13850|Humanoid-Hanoi]] · [[2511.17925|Switch-JustDance]] · [[2602.21599|Iterative Closed-Loop]] · [[2507.18883|Partial-Obs Loco]] · [[2307.10142|Potential-Based Rewards]] · [[2408.00342|MuJoCo-MPC-HB]]","x":60,"y":2680,"width":560,"height":178,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"a600000000000002","type":"text","text":"**Base↔arm — humanoid mobile-manipulation** 🟧 *main test*\n[[2407.07788|BiGym]] (Unitree H1) · [[2503.05652|BRS]] (Galaxea R1).\n\n*The common mobile-manip benchmarks are non-humanoid, so I don't use them.*","x":660,"y":2682,"width":560,"height":176,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"a600000000000003","type":"text","text":"**Holding a load — force & contact** 🟧 *main test*\n[[2505.06776|FALCON]] force curriculum · [[2510.26280|Thor]] (167 N pull) · [[2606.03297|SplitAdapter]] (6 kg) · contact force on [[2604.13015|Touch Dreaming]] (real, with / without touch) + [[2403.10506|HumanoidBench]] touch arm · [[2510.25725|Humanoid Visual-Tactile-Action]] (touch dataset).","x":1260,"y":2682,"width":560,"height":178,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"plnote0000000001","type":"text","text":"**Every step has a go / no-go.** If a step fails you still get a clear result (the ablation, or the ε-curve) — so **no branch is wasted.**","x":840,"y":2420,"width":560,"height":72,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"a600000000000004","type":"text","text":"**Real-robot sim-to-real (humanoid)** — [[2602.01515|RAPT]], tested on the real H1 / G1 robots.","x":60,"y":2880,"width":560,"height":80},
		{"id":"a600000000000005","type":"text","text":"**The backbone test** — run each backbone (a simple PPO baseline, [[2411.04983|DINO-WM]], [[2504.02792|UWM]], [[2501.03575|Cosmos]], [[2603.14482|V-JEPA 2.1]]) with the coupling **off vs on**. Same backbone, off vs on, proves the gain comes from the coupling, not the backbone.","x":60,"y":2980,"width":560,"height":120},
		{"id":"a800000000000000","type":"text","text":"*Speaker note: I want your sign-off on the direction before I commit the next phase, and a steer on sequencing.*","x":60,"y":3140,"width":1760,"height":60},
		{"id":"a800000000000002","type":"text","text":"**Cross-references**\n• [[Focus-Direction]] — the explicit-coupling thesis this pitch reduces from\n• [[Focus-Direction-Research-Plan]] + [[Focus-Direction-Research-Plan-detailed]] — lean & full-rigor plans\n• [[Focus-Direction-Paper-Code-Index]] — every cited paper → KH note + cloned repo\n• Source clusters: [[Whole-Body]] (A / B / C), [[WAM]] (predict), [[Sim2Real]] (ground), [[Embodied-AI]] (verify)","x":960,"y":3230,"width":860,"height":260},
		{"id":"f0000000000000g1","type":"text","text":"## ① The goal\n**Make humanoid robots better at using their whole body at once.**\n\n*A university lab can't out-scale industry on data or compute, so the edge has to be a smarter idea.*","x":100,"y":40,"width":400,"height":200,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"f0000000000000g2","type":"text","text":"## ② What I noticed\n*after reading ~180 papers (surveys + methods)*\n\n**Robots run the arm and the legs as two separate systems, and ignore how they push on each other.**","x":780,"y":40,"width":400,"height":200,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"f0000000000000g3","type":"text","text":"## ③ The insight\n**The body's physics says that push is real, and you can calculate it.**\n\n*So it is something to **predict** — not learn from piles of data.*","x":1500,"y":40,"width":400,"height":200,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"f0000000000000g4","type":"text","text":"## ④ The gap\n**Everyone reacts to that push too late, hides it, or handles only one direction.**\n\n*No one predicts it ahead of time.*","x":2240,"y":40,"width":400,"height":200,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"gfl000210000000","type":"text","text":"**[[2505.06776|FALCON]]** · *reacts late*\nTwo agents share a force curriculum to carry loads.\n→ but compensate **after** feeling the force, never brace ahead.","x":-130,"y":1702,"width":460,"height":120,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"gfl000210000001","type":"text","text":"**[[2201.03871|ALMA]]** · *known loads only*\nAnticipates the wrench from its **own** known motion, on a quadruped.\n→ but can't handle an unknown external load; separate policy.","x":350,"y":1702,"width":460,"height":158,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"gfg000210000000","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2505.06776-method.png","x":-130,"y":1840,"width":239,"height":150},
		{"id":"gch0000000002100","type":"text","text":"### holding a load","x":-130,"y":1620,"width":940,"height":60,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"plc2000000000001","type":"text","text":"**Later (deferred)**\nA certified safe limit that guarantees balance + no collisions under load.","x":1920,"y":2260,"width":380,"height":100,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"prob000000000001","type":"text","text":"# ⚑ THE PROBLEM\n**Humanoid robots ignore how the arm, base, and legs push on each other.**\nToday this push is handled *late, hidden, or only one way* — **never predicted ahead of time inside one controller.**","x":1300,"y":560,"width":560,"height":180,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"gfg000124000001","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2401.02117-method.png","x":350,"y":1240,"width":459,"height":140},
		{"id":"gfg000124000000","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2507.01961-method.png","x":-130,"y":1240,"width":459,"height":336},
		{"id":"gfg000210000001","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2201.03871-method.png","x":350,"y":1880,"width":436,"height":150},
		{"id":"gfl000038000000","type":"text","text":"**[[2604.07993|HEX]]** · *hides the link*\nA mixture-of-experts policy that *learns* the arm-leg push.\n→ but never writes it as a clear predicted number, so you can't plan against it.","x":-130,"y":640,"width":460,"height":120,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"gch0000000000380","type":"text","text":"### arm ↔ leg","x":-130,"y":560,"width":940,"height":60,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"gaphdr0000000001","type":"text","text":"## The gap — how the field handles this push **today**\n*close to the goal, but each one leaves room to improve*","x":-130,"y":440,"width":940,"height":100,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"gfl000124000000","type":"text","text":"**[[2507.01961|AC-DiT]]** · *one way only*\nConditions the arm's action on the base's motion.\n→ but only base→arm; the arm never steers the base back.","x":-130,"y":1100,"width":460,"height":120,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"gfl000124000001","type":"text","text":"**[[2401.02117|Mobile ALOHA]]** · *lumped together*\nImitation on a mobile two-arm robot; base + arm stacked into one command.\n→ so the base-arm link just drifts, no structure.","x":350,"y":1100,"width":460,"height":120,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"gch0000000001240","type":"text","text":"### base ↔ arm","x":-130,"y":1020,"width":940,"height":60,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"gfl000038000001","type":"text","text":"**[[2606.16542|ADAPT]]** · *reacts late*\nA disturbance observer estimates the push from sensors, online.\n→ but only **after** it happens, never before.","x":350,"y":640,"width":460,"height":120,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"gfg000038000000","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2604.07993-method.png","x":-130,"y":780,"width":459,"height":136},
		{"id":"gfg000038000001","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2606.16542-method.png","x":350,"y":780,"width":460,"height":208},
		{"id":"a300000000000011","type":"text","text":"**WB.A2 · BlendBridge**\n[[2506.09366|SkillBlender]] + [[2602.08594|MOSAIC]] + [[2602.06341|HiWET]]\n*Blend ready-made skills; a gated per-joint residual fixes the gaps for the real robot.*","x":3620,"y":320,"width":320,"height":140},
		{"id":"a300000000000021","type":"text","text":"**WB.B2 · LookAhead**\n[[2603.03243|HoMMI]] + [[2405.07991|SPIN]] + [[2411.04999|DynaMem]]\n*Decide where to look together with where to move the base, in one chunk.*","x":3620,"y":580,"width":320,"height":140},
		{"id":"a300000000000031","type":"text","text":"**WB.C2 · PALADIN**\n[[2605.25546|ISSf-CBF]] + [[2604.07457|CMP]] + [[2602.01515|RAPT]]\n*Turn that prediction into a safety limit that keeps balance under load.*","x":3640,"y":840,"width":320,"height":140},
		{"id":"a300000000000012","type":"text","text":"**WB.A3 · ReachSched**\n[[2602.06341|HiWET]] + [[2508.11275|Diff. Reachability]]\n*Move the base along a reach-map so the arm can always reach, correcting as it goes.*","x":3960,"y":320,"width":320,"height":140},
		{"id":"a300000000000022","type":"text","text":"**WB.B3 · EchoPurge**\n[[2511.18112|EchoVLA]] + [[2411.04999|DynaMem]] + [[2510.07134|TrackVLA++]]\n*Remember the room and fix wrong memories on the fly.*","x":3960,"y":580,"width":320,"height":140},
		{"id":"a300000000000013","type":"text","text":"**WB.A4 · CoLA-WB**\n[[2512.11047|WholeBodyVLA]] + [[2506.13751|LeVERB]] + [[2606.18772|HALOMI]]\n*Turn one whole-body command into leg + arm motions that are always doable.*","x":4300,"y":320,"width":320,"height":140},
		{"id":"a300000000000041","type":"text","text":"**WAM.A2 · WrenchCast**\n[[2606.09337|TORL-VLA]] + [[2606.13877|ContactWorld]] + [[2603.17851|DexViTac]]\n*Imagine the forces a few steps ahead, with no force sensor.*","x":3626,"y":1100,"width":314,"height":160}
	],
	"edges":[
